                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alan Wake is not your typical action game; it is a bizarre, psychological horror experience defined by an incredible atmosphere and a brilliant, cinematic, TV-style narrative that leaves you on edge at the end of every chapter. The game thrives on its own obscurity and beautiful weirdness, balancing its high tension with perfectly spaced, logical save points. Its combat mechanics are incredibly unique, forcing you to use your flashlight as a crosshair to blind swarming enemies and conserve ammo, which helps balance the struggle of managing Alan's frustratingly slow stamina and sprinting speed. Supported by amazing retro audio design, the game features exceptionally creative yet simple boss fights with Episode 4 being an absolute standout. Overall, it is an amazing, absurd ride that earns a well-deserved 8/10 and is well worth revisiting.",
